From 3b504821c353ec3f577d31fb386d353ea0044e42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:39:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ggml-cpu): list live KV tiles in sparse prefill to match
 the tiled path bit for bit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sparse prefill path packed the live cells of a token group into
64-wide tiles. Its online softmax then summed other tiles than the dense
tiled path, so the result was only close to it. On Qwen3.8-Flash-Next
Q8_0 (wiki.test.raw, -c 4608, 2 chunks) the cell lists gave a mean KLD
of 0.005041 and a same top p of 99.066% against the U4 build.

Phase 1 now lists the aligned 64-cell tiles in which any of the group's
8 rows sees a cell. Phase 2 packs a listed tile as the tiled path does,
so each row sums the same tiles, with the same lanes and the same FMA
order. A tile the list drops is dead for every row of the group, and the
tiled path skips a dead tile for a row without changing S, M or VKQ.

A list now holds at most every tile, so it cannot overflow. The size
helper loses the n_kv_max argument, and the fallback for an overflowed
list and the debug check of the hint contract go.

test_flash_attn_ext_sparse_exact outputs the hinted op minus the same op
without the hint, on a mask built as qwen4exp builds its QSA mask
(init_tensor_kq_mask_qsa). The CPU must give exactly zero.

Checks, with the dump and cmp harness on the CPU backend:
- The 5 new cases dump exactly +0.0 at 32 and 16 threads, and all 5 take
  the sparse path. The cell list libraries give nonzero output in 4 of 5
  (max abs 2.6e-08 to 6.0e-08). The fifth sees only tile 0.
- All 5338 FLASH_ATTN_EXT cases are bit-exact against the U4 libraries,
  at 32 and at 16 threads.
- llama-perplexity with the settings above writes a KL divergence base
  file byte-identical to the U4 one. The KLD statistics match those of
  U4 against itself.

The live tile fraction on that model is 0.942 (48 ops), against a live
cell fraction of 0.694 for the cell lists, so this path reads more K/V
than the cell lists did.

